  <!-- Chapter 21 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch21"
    number={21}
    title="Sand Fortress (Alternate Chapter 1)"
    timeline="Alternate"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="24"
      party="Stocke, Raynie, Rosch"
      
      enemies={[{"name": "Granorg Archer"}, {"name": "Light Granorgite"}, {"name": "Red Cap"}]}
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
<AsciiMap>
<pre>_________________
   Sand Fortress N     2F |     B           |     S - Save Point
                          |   ___ ___ ___   |     X - Obstacle
    __       |  |        _|  |   |   |   |  |_    B - Bomb
   /  \     /    \      |    |   |   |B  |  X |   1 - Emerald
  |    |   /      |     |    |   |___|   |  X4|   2 - 2000 G
  |XXXX|  |      /      |_   | 3 |   |   |  X_|   3 - Panacea Plus
  |    |__|     |___      |  |_ _|   |_ _|  |     4 - Mana Crystal x2
  |                7\     |          S      |     5 - Leaf Ring
   \_____     ______/     |______     ______|     6 - Darkshield Scroll
         |   |                   |   |            7 - 2000 G</pre>
</AsciiMap>

<p>___|   |___          _____ ___________   3F |           |     1F |   X2|     | B   |      |          6|        |__ X_|__ __|__ __|      |___     ___|        | B               |    ______|   |______      |_____________ ___|     If you have learned the Mana   |5X   _______     |     |     |     |     |     Sight ability, you can   |_X___ _____   ___|     |     |_| |_|     |     continue with the plot from   |B    |_____|     |     |      S        1 |     here.  In addition to the   |______     ______|     |______     ______|     bombs, you can also find much          |   |                   |   |            hidden treasure here.</p>

<p>On the first floor, search the lower right corner for a chest which contains an EMERALD (Poison Res +6).  I&#x27;m not a fan of status resisting equipment, so I would just sell it.  Head to the upper right room and search the upper left corner for a white sparkle that is your first bomb to disarm.  Go left in the hallway until you find the second bomb.  In the upper left room, pull the crates out that block a hidden chest which contains 2000 G.  Now, head up to the second floor.</p>

<p>Search the room on the right for a bomb in the upper left corner.  The room to the left holds a hidden chest which contains a PANACEA PLUS.  Leave the room and walk around the back side to find the fourth bomb.  On the right side of the floor are some crates that you can pull, blocking a hidden chest which contains 2 MANA CRYSTALS.  Head up to the third floor.</p>

<p>In the upper left corner is the last bomb, but you should still collect some more treasure.  Walk around to the right, but don&#x27;t go up the stairs.  Pull the crates to the left out of the way that are blocking a chest which contains a LEAF RING (HP+10/MP+10, sell).  Climb the stairs and go up to the large room. Search the right side for a hidden chest which contains the DARKSHIELD SCROLL for Raynie.  Don&#x27;t teach to Raynie right now, or you will have the find the bombs all over again.</p>

<p>Proceed up to the Sand Fortress North area.  In the lower right corner is a hidden chest which contains 2000 G.  Now, you should report to Rosch and choose to &quot;Prioritize the Mission&quot; to proceed with the plot, now that the bombs are out of the way.</p>

<Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
<p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game<br/>Stocke: Rune Edge, Heavy Mail, Fang Charm x3<br/>Raynie: Rune Spear, Heavy Mail, Horn Charm x3<br/>Marco: Wisp Blade, Heavy Mail, Bishop Stud, Knight Stud x2<br/>Rosch: P.Thauma Spear, Mail Vest, Wind Armlet, Fang Charm x2<br/>Extra: Rhapsody, Rune Claw</p>
</Callout>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Sand Fortress Battle">
<p>You should know your way around here pretty well by now.  I&#x27;d recommend fighting all the enemies you can find on all three floors.  Note the soldiers will never spawn in a room.  When you&#x27;ve killed enough of them to satisfy your bloodlust, make your way up to the upper room on the third floor to make your last stand.  I&#x27;d recommend giving Raynie&#x27;s Horn Charms to Stocke, and having Marco replace her.  You may also want to remove Rosch&#x27;s Wind Armlet, since you won&#x27;t have a chance to equip it on someone else later.</p>
</Callout>

<p>******************************************************************************* BOSS TIME: Grey Shadow, Granorg Archer x2, Light Granorgite WEAKNESS: None STRATEGY: The Grey Shadow will always start the battle with a Power Zone.  If anyone steps on it, absolutely get them off of it as quickly as possible or they will kill you.  Your first priority should be to take out the Grey Shadow, since that will clear the Power Zone.  If you have any full Mana Burst gauges, use Turn Break on the Grey Shadow, whenever his turn comes around.  In the first round, have Marco use Magic Boost on either Stocke or Raynie.  A couple spells and physical attacks should finish him off.  The rest can be handled easily without the need for further buffing or healing. *******************************************************************************</p>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: A Message from Home">
<p>After some cutscenes, you will hear about your next mission.</p>
</Callout>

<Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
<p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game<br/>Stocke: Rune Edge, Heavy Mail, Fang Charm x3<br/>Raynie: Rune Spear, Heavy Mail, Horn Charm x3<br/>Marco: Wisp Blade, Heavy Mail, Bishop Stud, Knight Stud x2<br/>Extra: Rhapsody, Rune Claw</p>
</Callout>

<p>=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=</p>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 22 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch22"
    number={22}
    title="Sand Fortress (Alternate Chapter 2)"
    timeline="Alternate"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="27"
      party="Stocke, Raynie, Marco"
      
      
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Alistel&#x27;s Offensive">
<p>After receiving your objective and destination, talk to Viola again to advance the [A Letter to Tomorrow] sidequest.  Return to the &quot;A New Mission&quot; node.  As long as we&#x27;re here, you can teach the Darkshield Scroll to Raynie.  Talk to Cedric, who is on the upper platform next to the tavern.  Choosing &quot;Don&#x27;t show journal&quot; will unlock the the [A Voice Unheard] ending.  Otherwise, choosing to &quot;Show Journal&quot; will complete the [A Letter to Tomorrow] sidequest and you will receive the NOAH AMULET (Poison/Sleep/Paralysis Res+4, sell).</p>
</Callout>

<p>Return to &quot;Alistel&#x27;s Offensive&quot; node.  Climb up to the third floor and take the north exit to the Gran Plain.</p>

<p>=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=</p>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 23 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch23"
    number={23}
    title="Gran Plain (Alternate Chapter 2)"
    timeline="Alternate"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="27"
      party="Stocke, Raynie, Marco"
      
      enemies={[{"name": "Blue Granorg Archer", "weakness": "Sleep"}, {"name": "Granorg Defender"}, {"name": "Hunter", "weakness": "Sleep"}]}
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Battle of Gran Plain">
<p>Go north one screen, west two, and continue west until you get an update on the battle situation here.  You will then have a decision to make.  Choosing to &quot;Go north&quot; will unlock [The Lion General] ending.</p>
</Callout>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: A Meeting Too Late">
<p>Before returning to this node, I would strongly recommend resting up in a bed on the second floor of the Sand Fortress.  Then, return to the decision point, this time choosing to &quot;Look for Rosch&quot;, and you will find him.</p>
</Callout>

<p>******************************************************************************* BOSS TIME: Blue Granorg Archer x3, Paelzan, Wood Shield x3 WEAKNESS: Sleep, None, Fire STRATEGY: During the first round, use Magic Boost on Raynie, cast Fire on the middle Wood Shield, and cast Magic Boost on Stocke.  In the second round, Push Assault Paelzan into the Blue Granorg Archer and two Fire spells should finish them off.  Next, have Marco heal as necessary, while Stocke and Raynie cast Fire on the Wood Shields.  Finally, use Right Assault and two Fire spells to finish off the remaining Blue Granorg Archers. *******************************************************************************</p>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Rosch in Crisis">
<p>[Wolf in the Fold node] Return to the &quot;Alistel&#x27;s Offensive&quot; node and talk to Viola to unlock the [Viola&#x27;s Decision] node.  Return to the &quot;A Meeting Too Late&quot; node and proceed as before until you are prompted with another decision.  Make sure to choose &quot;I leave it to you.&quot;, as this is a requirement to unlocking the sidequest [At Journey&#x27;s End] later.</p>
</Callout>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Lives Entrusted">
<p>After the battle, the plot will return to Alistel.</p>
</Callout>

<p>=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=</p>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 24 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch24"
    number={24}
    title="Alistel (Alternate Chapter 2)"
    timeline="Alternate"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="30"
      party="Stocke"
      
      
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Homecoming">
<p>Before inspecting Hugo&#x27;s office, take the elevator down to the first floor. Talk to the receptionist behind the left desk to receive the [Swordsman Recuit] and [Mercenary Recruit] sidequests, though you won&#x27;t be able to complete them for a very long time.  Return to the third floor, and enter Hugo&#x27;s office to the left where you will find someone other than Hugo.</p>
</Callout>

<p>******************************************************************************* BOSS TIME: Heiss WEAKNESS: None STRATEGY: Use the Change command to string together four consecutive turns of Fire spells to defeat him. *******************************************************************************</p>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Parting Ways">
<p>For winning the battle, Stocke will learn the Vanish technique, that can allow him to sneak past enemies without being seen.  This includes the guards back at Granorg Palace.  If you want to go back there now, then skip ahead to Chapter 29 (Granorg Palace), but I wouldn&#x27;t do that right now.</p>
</Callout>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Flight">
<p>Talk to Sonja in the infirmary to make your escape before you get caught.</p>
</Callout>

<p>******************************************************************************* BOSS TIME: Special Forces x2 WEAKNESS: None STRATEGY: One of them will start with Power Zone.  Do everything you can to keep them off of it.  As long as you do that, they can&#x27;t really hurt you much. Casting Fire two or three time is your best bet for killing each of them. *******************************************************************************</p>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Fiendish">
<p>After the battle, someone you haven&#x27;t seen before finds you.</p>
</Callout>

<p>=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=</p>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

