    id="ch28"
    number={28}
    title="Celestia (Alternate Chapter 3)"
    timeline="Alternate"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="33"
      party="Stocke, Raynie, Marco"
      
      
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
<p>Upon entering, you will find that you are a little late to the party.</p>

<p>******************************************************************************* BOSS TIME: Alistel Soldier x2, Auto Defender x2 WEAKNESS: Sleep, Fire STRATEGY: Use two Sleep Wings to crowd control the soldiers.  Sadly, the Auto Defenders cannot be moved.  Have Marco cast Magic Boost on Raynie and Stocke. Use Stocke&#x27;s Air Assault on one Auto Defender, followed up by G-Fire from Raynie to finish it off, and repeat on the second one.  Finally, use the Change command to set up a Push Assault, Air Assault, G-Fire, and some attacks to finish off the rest. *******************************************************************************</p>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Premonition of War">
<p>After some scenes, talk to Rosch at the Boundary Tree, then return to talk to Raul.  Talk to Barranca to decide what to do about Alistel and who should lead. Choosing to &quot;Nominate Raul&quot; will unlock the [Assassination of Raul] ending.</p>
</Callout>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Shattered Steel Arm">
<p>Return to this node and advance the plot up to the same decision.  However, choosing to &quot;Nominate Rosch&quot; will only lead to a dead end.</p>
</Callout>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Rosch in Agony">
<p>If you&#x27;ve already resolved this roadblock, then skip ahead to Chapter 36 (Celestia - Alternate Chapter 3).  Otherwise, you will need return to the &quot;How to Disappear&quot; node in Standard History to put the Vanish ability to use.</p>
</Callout>

<p>Before doing that, this is as good a time as any to complete those sidequests we got back at Alistel.  Unfortunately, it will involve going through half of Chapter 3 to get back there to complete them.  However, the rewards are good.</p>

<p>Return to the &quot;A New Mission&quot; node.  Climb the stairs by the tavern and talk to the man above to advance the [Second Opinion] sidequest.  Return to &quot;The Valkyrie&quot; node and head up to Rosch and Viola in the middle room above. Talk to the soldier sitting on the bench to advance the [Battlefield Missive] sidequests and receive the DEATH PACT for Stocke later.  Now for the hard part.</p>

<p>The nearest node to complete these sidequests is &quot;The Beastkind Forest&quot; node. Advance the plot to the &quot;Darkness in Alistel&quot; node.  Talk to the boy by the weapon shop to complete the [Battlefield Missive] sidequest and receive a CELESTIAL OIL.  Head left to the bar. This time, the man will have survived. Talk to him to complete the [Second Opinion] sidequest and receive the SLUMBERING SCROLL for Raynie, which you should teach her immediately.  Finally, return to the &quot;How to Disappear&quot; node to continue the plot.</p>

<Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
<p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game<br/>Stocke: Sorcery Epee, Heavy Mail, Fang Charm x3<br/>Raynie: Magic Spear, Heavy Mail, Crystal Charm, Thaumatech Orb, Horn Charm<br/>Marco: Wisp Blade, Heavy Mail, Bishop Stud x3<br/>Aht: Rhapsody, Reinforced Cape, Bishop Stud x3<br/>Gafka: Rune Claw, Leather Cuirass, Fang Charm x3<br/>Extra: Horn Charm x6</p>
</Callout>

<p>=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=</p>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

